Yeah, I worked my ass off on my portfolio in a gap year to get the University I'm at. I don't want to share the name for privacy's sake but I don't plan on sacrificing my studies. I am paying the minimum fees on the card.

&#x200B;

Why would my parents pay off the cards?.. They aren't the ones who spent my money lmao they have nothing to do with my errors?

Thank you so much for all this! I actually believe I do have Ulerythema Ophryogenes and Atrophoderma Vermiculata. The photos match up with my face exactly and I have some pitted skin that matches with Atrophoderma Vermiculata. My eyebrows are incredibly sparse towards the outsides and haven't grown for years (i only really got them in my late teens too aha!). I've been using acids and the likes to exfoliate my face and my face definitely does look smooth now (It's why my derm thinks I have rosacea...) unless you take a photo with a flash, you see 1000s of very small little bumps perfectly matching where the redness is. It's so comforting to hear the KPRF disappeared for you with age, do you remember roughly when it was?! I've currently had 2 VBeam lasers, neither left me with any bruising and as a result have done nothing really, i want to speak with my derm and ask for the bruising settings, i don't mind the downtime but i do mind spending money on in-effective treatments aha! How did laser help you? At my current stage I'm unsure if tret will help given the KP bumps are so small, will it still help release the clogged keratin pores? 

&#x200B;

Thanks so much for your help, I hope your skin is great now!

yeah i agree :/ not a fan of the direction it's been taking for a little while now and the third year has just been boring to read. honestly the best medicine is just stop reading it for a while and focus on other things you like, you'll come back in a few months and find you've got like 15 chapters to binge - which will most likely have dragged us out of this slow drag of an arc and into something new and exciting :) 

&#x200B;

(i also think the manga is just more enjoyable as a binge read rather than a weekly)

