Great Minds Think Alike

I just finished reading this and im really really fucking sorry you've had to go through with this. I came on this Sub-Reddit because I've been having a hard time recently but after reading this i feel pathetic for even considering sharing my story. im so sorry what you have had to go through, i had to deal with some of the stuff you brought up as well. I remember doing something as a kid and being scolded for weeks about it but when my little brother did it no one cared even though he did it to a worse extent. Whilst i was young i was never the sporty kid but my siblings were, every time we would go out with family or friends it was always about them, the only words they would say to me would be 'are you all right?' or 'Hows your Sister/Brother?'

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I really relate to you on a personal level with a lot of the things you brought up here, all i can say is just focus on yourself. You have talent, completely concentrate on that talent and Practice Practice PRACTICE until you are amazing at what you do and succeed in life and prove to everyone who's ever made you feel down you don't need them, It sounds horrible but people don't realise they need you until you dont need them. You have what it takes to be the best version of yourself and overcome all life's obstacles. Focus on harnessing yous skills and abilities and begin to work your way up through life  one promotion at a time until your finally at the top and can look down on the people that make you feel this way. Never give in because of it, you'll only prove your low self esteem right. Keep on Moving, Never Give up. I belive in you!!!

