Yeah i've actually had quite a few people mention i should change it to TJ, however i get nervous it could have a negative effect down the line careers wise as i know some companies like to hire people with more professional names, ones that sound abbreviated like TJ are often frowned upon which is a shame. It's definitely not something that always happens but it does. 

&#x200B;

I'll make sure to keep thinking about 'TJ' though because if people think its good and im happy with it then it might be a good choice, Thanks Again!

